agg AggregateStopLoss
  100 claims
  1000 xs 0
  sev lognorm 100 cv 1.5
  poisson
  aggregate net of
    5000 xs 30000
  note{Aggregate stop-loss -- net of an annual 5000-xs-30000 layer.}
  tags{topic:reinsurance};

agg OccurrenceXOL
  15 claims
  10000 xs 0
  sev lognorm 1500 cv 1
  occurrence net of
    50% po 2500 xs 2500 and
    90% po 5000 xs 5000
  mixed gamma 0.25
  note{Occurrence excess-of-loss program, net view.}
  tags{topic:reinsurance, check:reconciliation}
  doc{{{
## Problem

You have a two-layer per-occurrence excess program with partial placements, and you want the *net* aggregate -- with gross and ceded still visible, so you can see where the cession went instead of taking the net on faith.

## Solution

```python
a = build('''<<decl>>''')
qd(a.reins_summary_df)
```

## Discussion

`occurrence net of ...` applies the program claim by claim, before the frequency convolution -- which is what "per occurrence" means and why it cannot be done by adjusting the aggregate afterwards.

`50% po 2500 xs 2500` cedes half of the 2500-excess-2500 layer, `90% po 5000 xs 5000` nine tenths of the layer above it; `and` chains them into one program.

Note the program above is the **canonical** form. A partial placement is written `po` (*part of*), and the leading quantity says which reading you mean: a percentage is the share directly, a bare number is an absolute amount and the share is that amount over the limit. Both normalize to the `<pct>% po <limit> xs <attach>` spelling you see here, because the spec stores only the resolved fraction. That is why what you wrote and what the library shows back can differ without anything having changed.

`reins_summary_df` is the exhibit that matters here: three stages (gross, ceded, net) x three components (freq, sev, agg), with theoretic `EX` next to the FFT `Est EX`. The frequency row is identical across the three views -- occurrence cover changes what each claim costs, never how many there are.

## Check

```python
# net + ceded = gross, on both severity and aggregate, to grid accuracy
est = a.reins_summary_df['Est EX'].xs('occ')
for component in ('sev', 'agg'):
    gross = est[('gross', component)]
    net = est[('net', component)]
    ceded = est[('ceded', component)]
    assert abs(net + ceded - gross) < 1e-6 * gross
# occurrence cover leaves the claim COUNT alone. Read this off the theoretic
# EX column: the gross frequency has no separate FFT estimate (Est EX is NaN
# there -- there is nothing to estimate, the count is an input).
ex = a.reins_summary_df['EX'].xs('occ')
assert abs(ex[('net', 'freq')] - ex[('gross', 'freq')]) < 1e-9
assert abs(ex[('ceded', 'freq')] - ex[('gross', 'freq')]) < 1e-9
```
}}};

